---
// src/pages/about.astro
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About — Monokai Blog">
  <main
    class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 flex-1 w-full min-w-0 space-y-10 font-mono"
  >
    {/* GNOME Terminal Window Header */}
    <div
      class="rounded-xl bg-monokai-dark border border-monokai-comment/30 overflow-hidden shadow-2xl"
    >
      <div
        class="bg-monokai-surface/70 px-4 py-3 flex items-center justify-between border-b border-monokai-comment/20"
      >
        <span class="text-xs text-monokai-comment select-none">
          bash — cat ~/about.txt
        </span>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-monokai-comment/50 inline-block"
          ></span>
          <span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-monokai-comment/50 inline-block"
          ></span>
          <span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-monokai-red inline-block"></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div
        class="p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6 text-sm sm:text-base text-monokai-text font-sans leading-relaxed"
      >
        {/* Intro Tag */}
        <div
          class="font-mono text-xs inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded bg-monokai-surface text-monokai-green border border-monokai-comment/40"
        >
          $ whoami
        </div>

        <h1
          class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight font-mono text-monokai-text"
        >
          Fixing things that aren't broken, building things that probably
          shouldn't exist.
        </h1>

        <p class="text-monokai-text/90">
          Welcome to <strong class="text-monokai-cyan font-mono"
            >Bare Metal Nerd</strong
          >.
        </p>

        <p class="text-monokai-text/90">
          I’m Fróes — an information security analyst by day, and a chaotic
          hardware/software tinkerer by heart. Have been breaking things for 15 years
          when taking it apart to see how it ticks (and spend days trying fixing it
          when it wouldn't work later).
        </p>

        {/* Section: The Stack / What I Do */}
        <div class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-monokai-comment/20">
          <h2
            class="text-lg font-mono text-monokai-yellow flex items-center gap-2"
          >
            <span class="text-monokai-red">&gt;</span> sys_specs & interests
          </h2>

          <ul
            class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-monokai-text/80"
          >
            <li
              class="p-3 rounded bg-monokai-surface/50 border border-monokai-comment/20 flex items-start gap-2"
            >
              <span class="text-monokai-green">•</span>
              <div>
                <strong class="text-monokai-text"
                  >Microcontrollers & SBCs:</strong
                > ESP32, Raspberry Pi, Milk-V Duo, and breathing new life into old
                discarded hardware.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li
              class="p-3 rounded bg-monokai-surface/50 border border-monokai-comment/20 flex items-start gap-2"
            >
              <span class="text-monokai-green">•</span>
              <div>
                <strong class="text-monokai-text"
                  >Linux & Custom Kernels:</strong
                > Chroot on toasters and water bottles, wrestling with dotfiles, and optimization
                rabbit holes.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li
              class="p-3 rounded bg-monokai-surface/50 border border-monokai-comment/20 flex items-start gap-2"
            >
              <span class="text-monokai-green">•</span>
              <div>
                <strong class="text-monokai-text">Cybersecurity:</strong> Defense
                engineering, SOC log analysis, penetration testing, and analyzing
                network traffic.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li
              class="p-3 rounded bg-monokai-surface/50 border border-monokai-comment/20 flex items-start gap-2"
            >
              <span class="text-monokai-green">•</span>
              <div>
                <strong class="text-monokai-text">Electronics & Bits:</strong> Soldering
                custom gadgets, digital dashboards, analog circuits, and custom peripherals.
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p class="text-monokai-text/80">
          This blog is essentially an unfiltered dump of my adventures,
          documentation for projects that went off the rails, and notes on how
          to keep ancient or unconventional tech running purely out of spite.
        </p>

        {/* Social Links Section */}
        <div
          class="space-y-3 pt-6 border-t border-monokai-comment/20 font-mono"
        >
          <div class="text-xs text-monokai-comment">
            # connect / source code / professional background
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-2">
            <a
              href="https://github.com/cauafroes"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="px-4 py-2.5 rounded-lg bg-monokai-surface hover:bg-monokai-comment/20 border border-monokai-comment/30 text-xs sm:text-sm text-monokai-cyan flex items-center gap-2 transition-all active:scale-95"
            >
              <span class="text-monokai-red">&gt;</span> github.com/cauafroes
            </a>

            <a
              href="https://br.linkedin.com/in/caua-froes"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="px-4 py-2.5 rounded-lg bg-monokai-surface hover:bg-monokai-comment/20 border border-monokai-comment/30 text-xs sm:text-sm text-monokai-orange flex items-center gap-2 transition-all active:scale-95"
            >
              <span class="text-monokai-red">&gt;</span> linkedin.com/in/caua-froes
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
